651
00:46:49,960 --> 00:46:52,980
to finish of how that worked.

652
00:46:56,520 --> 00:47:01,380
So from our React component,
our index in this case--

653
00:47:01,380 --> 00:47:05,880
it could be whatever component
you have your form in--

654
00:47:05,880 --> 00:47:09,380
we get our user
data from our form.

655
00:47:09,380 --> 00:47:11,880
And I just have it here.

656
00:47:11,880 --> 00:47:16,020
We pass that user data
to our createUser.

657
00:47:16,020 --> 00:47:20,600
And this is no longer a Redux
action, this is a thunk.

658
00:47:20,600 --> 00:47:23,240
We're passing that to
our thunk, but we still

659
00:47:23,240 --> 00:47:27,600
have to dispatch it with
dispatch, which we import

660
00:47:27,600 --> 00:47:31,620
from useDispatch, react-redux.

661
00:47:31,620 --> 00:47:36,560
UseDispatch makes
a dispatch function

662
00:47:36,560 --> 00:47:41,680
that we pass our createUser
thunk with our data to.

663
00:47:41,680 --> 00:47:46,440
That createUser thunk
is inside of our slice

664
00:47:46,440 --> 00:47:53,420
now, which is dispatching--
or it's fetching,

665
00:47:53,420 --> 00:47:58,120
it's creating a fetch
request at our endpoint

666
00:47:58,120 --> 00:48:01,300
here as a POST request.

667
00:48:01,300 --> 00:48:04,880
Remember, a POST request
always include data

668
00:48:04,880 --> 00:48:07,720
that we are sending
in the request.

669
00:48:07,720 --> 00:48:10,920
And that data here
is in the body.

670
00:48:10,920 --> 00:48:12,500
And we're sending JSON data.

671
00:48:12,500 --> 00:48:17,260
So in our headers, Content-Type
is application/json.

672
00:48:17,260 --> 00:48:21,960
Our body has our JSON body.

673
00:48:21,960 --> 00:48:27,780
And you can't just send
the JSON object directly,

674
00:48:27,780 --> 00:48:30,240
you have to send it as a string.

675
00:48:30,240 --> 00:48:33,440
And that has to do
with the way the data

676
00:48:33,440 --> 00:48:36,500
is serialized when it's
passed in the network request.

677
00:48:39,360 --> 00:48:43,040
So at this point, it gets--

678
00:48:43,040 --> 00:48:49,140
the fetch request will push
that data to the backend block.

679
00:48:49,140 --> 00:48:55,640
At this point, this is,
from here on, asynchronous.

680
00:48:55,640 --> 00:48:59,300
So the JavaScript code stops
executing at this point.

681
00:48:59,300 --> 00:49:00,720
It's waiting.

682
00:49:00,720 --> 00:49:04,360
And we go to Django.

